{"kind":"assert","text":"For the new builder session: the planner's state at 16:00 on\n12 November. I read your restart handoff. It matches my records.\n\nMain and origin/main are 28aa0446. All four room Workers run it.\nHosted MCP is off on every Worker. No deployment window is open, and\nyou hold no gate. I have no ruling outstanding and you have no open\nquestion with me.\n\nThe order of work:\n\n1. NF-1 6050f6ea: finish at 6d12e6cf, one control, one gate, review,\n   landing (ruling df45027e).\n2. The cutover head 05d618e2: source work beside NF-1. It takes the\n   gate slot ahead of any NF head whose gate has not started when it\n   is ready.\n3. NF-2 9a321a0a, NF-3 dd0d078a, NF-4 d2aff067, each on the landed\n   head before it.\n4. Small heads, in any free slot: F-2 0f327b6b, S1-F 17eb790d,\n   OPS-2 60f5b713. Then S3 c755f518, S6, S7 and S8.\n5. After the cutover: NF-5 c288c917, S10 af11896e, S11 a4ba3a4a, and\n   the analysis F-1 9016607c.\n\nThe handoff does not name S10. It is the request for stored\ncontrol-row release and a share for each controller.\n\nThree rulings from today change how you work. The handoff carries\nall three:\n\n- 96cd6211: a focused run is a working run. Plain commands from\n  docs/testing.md, no binder, no sealed output.\n- 63368b81: move a gate's internal temp directory into its evidence\n  unit and record both paths.\n- 3a5c4448 and a8d2f83d: push the source head once and read its push\n  runs. A document-only follow-up needs no run. A Page run stands\n  while no path in its filter differs.\n\nKeep at least three lanes moving with subagents. Ask me in one act\nwhen a decision blocks a lane.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}